926 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 556 0 R
/T (Animal agriculture can also have significant ethical challenges for human and animal welfare. Research has shown that slaughterhouse workers face elevated rates of mental health issues, including depression and anxiety, as well as violence-supportive attitudes2. There are notable humane concerns about the welfare of animals in agricultural systems, as they are often  subjected to intense living conditions and show signs of distress3. )
/E (Animal agriculture can also have significant ethical challenges for human and animal welfare. Research has shown that slaughterhouse workers face elevated rates of mental health issues, including depression and anxiety, as well as violence-supportive attitudes2. There are notable humane concerns about the welfare of animals in agricultural systems, as they are often  subjected to intense living conditions and show signs of distress3. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [3 6 4 7 5]
>>
endobj
927 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 556 0 R
/T (Sustainability in dining can mean many things depending on how it is assessed. One way that UCB determines the sustainability of procurement practices is through annual reporting of plant-based spend. This is an important metric, because animal-based agriculture can have serious environmental costs. Animal agriculture is responsible for 14.5% of global greenhouse gas emissions1, which are an important contributor to global warming and biodiversity loss. )
/E (Sustainability in dining can mean many things depending on how it is assessed. One way that UCB determines the sustainability of procurement practices is through annual reporting of plant-based spend. This is an important metric, because animal-based agriculture can have serious environmental costs. Animal agriculture is responsible for 14.5% of global greenhouse gas emissions1, which are an important contributor to global warming and biodiversity loss. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [8 10 9]
>>
endobj
928 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 556 0 R
/T (As an institution, it is important to promote values-based purchasing while also providing students with options that suit their diverse preferences. Institutional support for providing plant-based choices should seek to expand the options of students rather than reducing their access to animal-based products, especially in light of student dietary needs, allergies, and cultural/ religious restrictions.)
/E (As an institution, it is important to promote values-based purchasing while also providing students with options that suit their diverse preferences. Institutional support for providing plant-based choices should seek to expand the options of students rather than reducing their access to animal-based products, especially in light of student dietary needs, allergies, and cultural/ religious restrictions.)
/Pg 29 0 R
