/T (Ultimately, although current sustainability standards do not fully address the many systemic injustices in the modern food system, we hope this toolkit will help bring UC campuses closer to achieving food justice. In order to advance access to healthy, affordable, and culturally appropriate food not only for our students, but also for everyone across the supply chain, we must recognize and address the extensive inequalities upstream, ranging from farmers to food service workers who are on the frontlines of this demanding food system. )
/E (Ultimately, although current sustainability standards do not fully address the many systemic injustices in the modern food system, we hope this toolkit will help bring UC campuses closer to achieving food justice. In order to advance access to healthy, affordable, and culturally appropriate food not only for our students, but also for everyone across the supply chain, we must recognize and address the extensive inequalities upstream, ranging from farmers to food service workers who are on the frontlines of this demanding food system. )
/Pg 60 0 R
/K [2]
