/Title (What does institutional purchasing power really mean? It means that when enough people are mobilized to demand better food systems, large institutions and corporations are encouraged to listen. This energy can be leveraged to drive real change in supply chains, demonstrating how reshaping demand can produce better outcomes in supply.)
